      {
        "id": "medivh",
        "name": "Medivh"
      },
      {
        "id": "ana",
        "name": "Ana"
      },
      {
        "id": "malfurion",
        "name": "Malfurion"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Heroes that displace enemies, like Garrosh and E.T.C. are excellent with Malthael, as they will ease the focus on a target, allowing Last Rites to execute it. One of Malthael's problems is that he takes too long to reduce an enemy's health to Last Rites's threshold, so he is great with Greymane's Cursed Bullet or with Tychus's The Bigger They Are....\n\nDue to how Malthael's damage and self sustain is completely tied to Soul Rip, he has excellent synergy with Heroes that can reduce his Cooldowns. While Ana with Nano Boost turns Malthael into an immortal killing machine, Malfurion can enhance his effectiveness very often through Innervate."
  },
  "counters": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "blaze",
        "name": "Blaze"
      },
      {
        "id": "falstad",
        "name": "Falstad"
      },
      {
        "id": "fenix",
        "name": "Fenix"
      },
      {
        "id": "lunara",
        "name": "Lunara"
      },
      {
        "id": "tracer",
        "name": "Tracer"
      },
      {
        "id": "valla",
        "name": "Valla"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "As a Bruiser with a rather telegraphed play style, Malthael is very vulnerable to any form of targeted crowd control. Furthermore, since his main gap closer, Wraith Strike, requires him to either attack or hit a slow skillshot, he is naturally bound to be kited by nimble ranged Heroes.\n\nAgainst experienced players, Blaze will be an excellent counter to Malthael. Bunker Drop cleanses Reaper's Mark from anyone that enters it. It also denies Last Rites's damage. Considering enemies will be inside bunker, Malthael's self-sustain will be very limited, as Malthael will not be able to use Soul Rip to sustain himself."
  },
